\n$$" 13194139535898 17592186045417 false] [17592186166644 1074 "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n2x-x^2 & = -(x^2 - 2x)\\[5pt]\n& = -(x^2 - 2\\cdot x + 1^2-1^2)\\[5pt]\n& = -((x-1)^2 - 1) \\[5pt]\n&= 1 - (x-1)^2\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{(x-1)\\sqrt{2x-x^2}} \\textrm{d}x  = \\int  \\dfrac{1}{(x-1)\\sqrt { 1-(x-1)^2 } }\t\\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u = x-1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=1\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x-1)\\sqrt{2x-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-1)\\sqrt{1-(x-1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535898 17592186045417 true] [17592186166645 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{4-(2x-2)^2} \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139535898 17592186045417 false] [17592186166645 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{4-(2x-2)^2} \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139535898 17592186045417 true] [17592186166645 1074 "First, we note that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{4-(2x-2)^2}\\textrm{d}x = \n\\int \\dfrac{1}{4-4(x-1)^2}\\textrm{d}x = \n\\dfrac{1}{4} {\\int}\\dfrac{1}{ 1 - (x-1)^2 }\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u = x-1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=1\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(x-1)}^{2}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $\\left|{x-1} \\right| >   1.$" 13194139535898 17592186045417 true] [17592186166645